    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Cal Raleigh** stands as our premier offensive anchor, boasting an elite score of 73.48. He benefits from the day\u2019s most favorable matchup against a pitcher with a ballooning 9.12 xERA, combined with a significant park factor boost. Similarly, **Dylan Beavers** (68.38) is a must-start; his profile is buoyed by a 14% park advantage and a favorable encounter with Hughes, positioning him as a high-upside play for both power and potential stolen base production. We are also leaning on **Bryce Harper**, whose 71.01 score is driven by his high xwOBA and a strong statistical edge against Rodriguez, making him the safest bet for run production in the heart of our order.\n\nConversely, we are exercising caution with several middle-tier options. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (53.54) and **JJ Bleday** (53.88) are facing stiff opposition that suppresses their raw scoring potential, though they remain viable due to their respective lineup spots. **Zack Gelof** (55.34) is a particularly interesting case; while his base projection is modest, his score was elevated by the favorable matchup against Gore and a distinct 85% stolen base probability against a slow-delivering pitcher, reinforcing our strategy of chasing efficiency in the scarcest category. **Jung Hoo Lee** (41.56) is our most marginal start, narrowly edging out remaining depth options despite a brutal matchup against the elite Skenes, where his score is heavily penalized by the pitcher\u2019s dominance and the opposition's elite defensive catcher.\n\nRegarding our bench, the decision to leave **Luis Arraez** in the UTIL slot at 56.19 highlights the congestion of our lineup; he was a close contender for a starting spot, but his platoon disadvantage against a left-handed starter capped his ceiling compared to the primary lineup. We are monitoring **Will Smith**'s ongoing IL status, and while **Justin Crawford**, **Daulton Varsho**, and **Tyler Freeman** are currently unavailable due to benching or minor league assignments, we remain prepared to rotate them in should roster spots open. No weather alerts are currently threatening our action, but keep a close eye on the late-afternoon lineups, as any shuffling of the order could necessitate a recalibration of our efficiency scores for **Gleyber Torres** and **Alex Freeland**.",
